;; memoryview: a port of CPython 3.14.10's Objects/memoryobject.c (queue 473, the main session's 456-1 (a); PY5e's
;; minimum, PY6a's casts and queues 249-304's fixes before it). A view is a Py_buffer (Buffer): its exporter's memory
;; (BufMem: a Go exporter's bytes, or the C world's address space for a C exporter's view, kept in place), the address
;; of its first item, its length in bytes, item size, format, shape, strides and suboffsets (PIL-style indirect
;; arrays), and the flags init_flags computes from them. Indexing, slicing (init_slice), tolist, tobytes in C, Fortran or
;; any order (PyBuffer_ToContiguous), cast (cast_to_1D, cast_to_ND), the comparisons (memory_richcompare: unpack_cmp's
;; native formats, the struct module's for any other), hash, count, index and memory_getbuf are memoryobject.c's
;; algorithms over that description. Ported from CPython 3.14.10; the PSF's license, LICENSE.md.

